# Highlighting

A vault to look at in the editor, and not a vault to read. Each card holds one
kind of thing the extension colours, so that a colour that is missing or wrong
is easy to find.

## Map

- [[cells]]: HQL cells of every kind, with their saved output
- [[languages]]: fences in the languages the editor ships a grammar for
- [[more-languages]]: fences in languages that need an extension, and in none
- [[fence-forms]]: every way to write a fence, and the forms that stay with Markdown
- [[links]]: links, embeds and anchors, alone on a line and inside a sentence
- [[catalog]]: the cards the cells read

## Files that are not cards

- `queries/catalog.hql`: a standalone HQL program that reads this vault
- `queries/shapes.hql`: HQL declarations only, a trait and its implementations
- `src/`: the same small program in Python, Rust and TypeScript

## What to look at

| Where | What should be coloured |
| --- | --- |
| A `.hql` file | Keywords, types, function names, strings, numbers, comments |
| An `hql` fence | The same, inside the card |
| The line that opens a cell | The language, the `#`, the mode, and each attribute |
| A `python#eval` fence | The body, as Python |
| A `kotlin` fence | The opening line only, until an extension for Kotlin is installed |
| An `hql:output` marker | The marker and its attributes |
